hemorrhage. An emergency-use program also supplied it to patients who could not receive blood. ... 2015 Orphan Drug Designation in sickle cell disease; facility expands Regulatory ... Raul Nogueira Director, UPMC Stroke Institute, University of Pittsburgh Medical Center\n\n# About Prolong\n\nA privately held biotech company in South Plainfield, New Jersey, that develops and manufactures its own drugs under one roof.\n\n## Our story\n\nIn the 1970s and '80s, Prolong's scientific founders helped develop PEGylation: a drug delivery technology that wraps a protein in polyethylene glycol to extend its lifespan in the body. At Enzon, the technique led to Adagen in 1990, the first approved PEGylated protein.\n\nProlong was founded to apply the same technique to hemoglobin.\n\nFor about a decade, PP-007, previously SANGUINATE®, was studied in sickle cell disease, severe anemia, kidney transplant and brain injury after hemorrhage. An emergency-use program also supplied it to patients who could not receive blood.\n\nThe turn to stroke came from numerous animal studies in addition to proof-of-concept observed in delayed cerebral ischemia, leading to HEMERA-1.\n\n## From Adagen to HEMERA-1\n\n  1. 1990 Adagen approved, the first PEGylated protein Origin\n  2. 2002 Prolong founded Founded\n  3. 2010 Moves into the South Plainfield facility Facility\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPP-007 | Prolong Pharmaceuticals (https://www.prolongpharma.com/pp-007)\nciteturn671search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; PP-007 (formerly SANGUINATE®) is PEGylated bovine carboxyhemoglobin, administered by IV infusion, in development for treating acute ischemic stroke. ...     Breakthrough Therapy (Apr 2026, acute ischemic stroke) · Fast Track (Oct 2024, acute ischemic stroke) · Orphan Drug (2015, sickle cell disease) ... It holds oxygen tightly (P50 about 12 mmHg, against 26 for red blood cells), so it releases it primarily where tissue is starved. ... 300+ across 12 clinical studies in stroke, sickle cell disease, severe anemia, kidney transplant and more.\n\n# PP-007\n\nPP-007 (formerly SANGUINATE®) is PEGylated bovine carboxyhemoglobin, administered by IV infusion, in development for treating acute ischemic stroke.\n\n## At a glance\n\nWhat it is\n    PEGylated bovine carboxyhemoglobin oxygen carrier\n\nLead indication\n    Acute ischemic stroke due to anterior large vessel occlusion (A-LVO), alongside standard of care\n\nStatus\n    Phase 1/2 (HEMERA-1) complete · Pivotal Phase 3 (HEMERA-2) planned\n\nFDA designations\n    Breakthrough Therapy (Apr 2026, acute ischemic stroke) · Fast Track (Oct 2024, acute ischemic stroke) · Orphan Drug (2015, sickle cell disease)\n\nHuman experience\n    Over 300 people dosed across 12+ clinical studies\n\nFormat\n    500 mL ready-to-use IV bag, stored at room temperature\n\n## Reopening the vessel is not the same as saving the brain\n\nStroke care has two treatments: clot-dissolving drugs (IV thrombolysis, since 1996) and clot removal (mechanical thrombectomy, since 2015). Even when clot removal works, many patients do not recover, due to challenges downstream.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProlong - Sanguinate (https://www.prolongpharma.com/sanguinate)\nciteturn671search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; The primary indication for PP-007 is acute ischemic stroke (AIS), caused by a blood clot blocking brain blood flow, leading to hypoxia and brain injury. ... Survival was significantly different among treatment groups (p < 0.01), where LRS, Hextend, and SANGUINATE^{®}-treated animals survived 16 ± 3.4,76 ± 11.1 and 193 ± 33.4 mins, respectively.\n\nOnly SANGUINATE^{®} produced a significant rise in tissue P_{ISF}O_{2} by two hours post-resuscitation (p < 0.01).\nAdvancing Therapeutics\n\n# Our Pipeline of Innovative Solutions\n\nPP-007 Sanguinate®\n\nPreclinical\n\nPhase I\n\nPhase II\n\nPhase III\n\nProlong’s lead biopharmaceutical pipeline candidate is PEGylated carboxyhemoglobin bovine (PCHB). PP-007's unique mechanism arises from its components as an acellular, dual-action carbon monoxide (CO) releasing molecule and an oxygen transfer agent.\n\n1\n\nDraw blood from Holstein Cows\n\n2\n\nIsolate & Purify Hemoglobin\n\nImage\n\n3\n\nPEGylate & Add Carbon Monoxide\n\n4\n\nPP-007 Administrable Via IV\n\nInnovative Treatment\n\n##### What is PP-007?\n\nPP-007 (PEGylated bovine carboxyhemoglobin) is a nano-sized oxygen carrier. The PEGfinity™ process combines hemoglobin with PEG, modifying its hemoglobin saturation profile to selectively oxygenate severely hypoxic tissue.\n\nTarget Condition\n\n##### Acute Ischemic Stroke\n\nThe primary indication for PP-007 is acute ischemic stroke (AIS), caused by a blood clot blocking brain blood flow, leading to hypoxia and brain injury. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTerms of Use | Prolong Pharmaceuticals (https://www.prolongpharma.com/terms)\nciteturn671search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; It is not intended to be, and should not be relied upon as medical advice or a recommendation for treatment. Always seek the advice of a physician or other qualified health care provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical condition or other medical issue. ... In particular, “Prolong Pharmaceuticals,” “SANGUINATE,” “EPEG” and the Prolong “P” logo are registered trademarks of Prolong Pharmaceuticals®.\nProlong undertakes no obligation to update any forward-looking statement, whether as a result of new information, future events or otherwise, except as required by law.\n\nCopyright and Trademarks. This website, and the information, text, graphics, images, videos, logos, software and other materials which it contains (collectively, the “Content”), are the property of Prolong or its licensors and are protected from unauthorized copying and disseminat